I keep typing (P) to Put on armor, or (T) to take off a ring
and the "That is a silly thing to wear" messages are starting 
to bother me.

I considering making a change to the commands on my version of
nethack to reduce the number of different letters for similar
functions.  I'm thinking of something like using (r) to read 
both scrolls and spell books. I haven't completely decided on
the final version, but I think something like this:

W : wear armor/rings/amulets
R : remove armor/rings/amulets

A further reduction in the number of commands could be:
w : wield a weapon, wear armor/rings/amulets
R : remove armor/rings/amulets/weapon
    ie: r (current weapon) instead of w-

I guess a further reduction to this would be to just use (a) to
apply ANYTHING (weapons/rings/amulets/scrolls/potions/...), and
let the game figure out what you mean by the context.  I think
this is a bit too generic even for me, but I don't like the
overlap between W/P and R/T.  Particularly R and T because
they're so close on the keyboard.

What do you think of this idea?
